<h1>Hello World</h1>
<p class="lead">Write, compile, and run your first toke program.</p>

<h2>The program</h2>
<p>Create a file called <code>hello.tk</code>:</p>

<pre><code>m=hello;
i=io:std.io;

f=main():i64{
  io.println("Hello, world!");
  &lt;0;
};</code></pre>

<p>Every toke file begins with a module declaration (<code>m=</code>). Imports use <code>i=alias:module.path;</code>. Functions are declared with <code>f=</code>. The <code>&lt;</code> operator returns a value.</p>

<h2>Compile and run</h2>

<pre><code>./build/tkc hello.tk -o hello
./hello</code></pre>

<p>Output:</p>

<pre><code>Hello, world!</code></pre>

<h2>Next: Fibonacci</h2>

<pre><code>m=fib;

f=fib(n:i64):i64{
  if(n&lt;2){&lt;n;};
  &lt;fib(n-1)+fib(n-2);
};

f=main():i64{
  &lt;fib(10);
};</code></pre>

<p>Run: <code>./fib; echo $?</code> → <code>55</code></p>

